  "id": "DrugBank_DB11363 - MONDO_8903",
  "verbalization": "Alectinib, a tyrosine kinase inhibitor, is associated with Non-small Cell Lung Carcinoma (NSCLC) through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Alectinib may exert its therapeutic effect on NSCLC by targeting pathways that are also implicated in other cancers, such as PD-1/PD-L1 signaling (via Pembrolizumab and Nivolumab) and glutathione synthesis (via Pemetrexed). These pathways are often involved in tumor progression and resistance, and their involvement in NSCLC highlights a potential mechanism by which Alectinib could influence disease progression. The presence of multiple pathways linking Alectinib to NSCLC underscores the complexity of its biological role and suggests that its therapeutic effect may be context-dependent. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Alectinib may have a role in the treatment of NSCLC, particularly in cases where these downstream targets are dysregulated.",
